invariant: INV-16
file: src/p256_wide_word.h
catches: p256_equiv_test_sum
reason: the 128-bit form of the masked subtraction takes its mask from bit 63
  of the 64-bit difference and not from the top word of the 128-bit one
  (docs/decisions.md 243). Where a and b differ by 2^63 or more, that bit is
  not the borrow, so the inverse's step swaps where it must not or keeps
  where it must swap, and the inverse comes out wrong.
  bin/p256_equiv_test_sum runs this form and holds every inverse on it to
  p256_field.c's and p256_scalar.c's.

--- old
    *mask = (uint64_t)(difference >> 64);
--- new
    *mask = p256_wide_mask_top((uint64_t)difference);
